<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Piura</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as San Miguel de Piura</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Piura is a city in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, near the Pacific coast. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a> in 1532 as San Miguel, it was the first Spanish city in Peru, set up before his march to meet the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atahualpa">Atahualpa</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cajamarca">Cajamarca</a>. Moved several times, it settled on its present site in 1588 and is now the capital of the Piura Region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/piura.jpg" alt="Piura" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edward Josué Quevedo Macalupú · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PLAZA_DE_ARMAS_DE_PIURA_-_PIURA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
